Let $p$ be a prime number. Consider the following valued fields, each equipped with its natural valuation:

(a) $\mathbb{Q}_p(\zeta_{p^\infty})$, the field obtained from the $p$-adic numbers $\mathbb{Q}_p$ by adjoining all $p$-power roots of unity;
(b) $\mathbb{Q}_p(p^{1/p^\infty})$, obtained from $\mathbb{Q}_p$ by adjoining a compatible system of $p$-power roots of $p$;
(c) $\mathbb{Q}_p^{\mathrm{ab}}$, the maximal abelian extension of $\mathbb{Q}_p$;
(d) $\mathbb{F}_p((t))^{1/p^\infty}$, the perfect hull of the formal Laurent series field $\mathbb{F}_p((t))$;
(e) $\mathbb{F}_p^{\mathrm{ac}}((t))^{1/p^\infty}$, the perfect hull of $\mathbb{F}_p^{\mathrm{ac}}((t))$, where $\mathbb{F}_p^{\mathrm{ac}}$ is an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{F}_p$.

Let $\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{val}}$ be the language of valued rings (the ring language together with a binary predicate or unary divisibility relation expressing the valuation), and let $\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{val}}(t) = \mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{val}} \cup \{t\}$ be its expansion by a constant symbol naming the uniformizer $t$.

Determine whether the complete theories of the structures in (a), (b), and (c) in the language $\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{val}}$ are decidable. Determine whether the complete theories of the structures in (d) and (e) are decidable in $\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{val}}$, and whether they are decidable in the richer language $\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{val}}(t)$.

